            <div xml:id="d709">

                <pb facs="0814" n="729" xml:id="pg729"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">823.00/270: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Callao-Lima</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Handley</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-07-13T15:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 13, 1919,
                                3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received July 14,
                            4.06 a.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Your July 12, 4 p.m. My interview with Leguia purely accidental. I called upon an
                    intimate friend, who is Leguia’s legal adviser, regarding recent events as many
                    conflicting reports were about. He invited me to go to the Palace with him where
                    he would endeavor to procure definite information. After his conversation with
                    Leguia the latter called me in as a friend. I particularly informed him my
                    presence was not official, but purely accidental, which he understood. The
                    Department’s instructions will be strictly observed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Handley</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
